From 9bd13cf0a50988526687e89467c448be3d38e3d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:52:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] MAINTAINERS: add the HiSilicon Festa PHY driver entry

The Festa Ethernet PHY integrated in the HiSilicon STB SoCs has no
maintainer entry.

Its microcode download and Wake-on-LAN paths are the parts that need a
listed reviewer.

Register the driver under netdev.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 MAINTAINERS | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -12039,6 +12039,12 @@ L:	dmaengine@vger.kernel.org
 S:	Maintained
 F:	drivers/dma/hisi_dma.c
 
+HISILICON FESTA PHY DRIVER
+M:	David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
+L:	netdev@vger.kernel.org
+S:	Maintained
+F:	drivers/net/phy/hisi-festa.c
+
 HISILICON GPIO DRIVER
 M:	Yang Shen <shenyang39@huawei.com>
 L:	linux-gpio@vger.kernel.org
